  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the Learning Environment at Islamic University in Uganda Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Special Context: The borrower is a private Islamic university in Uganda, established by the Organization of Islamic Cooperation (OIC). Due to its private status, a government guarantee was necessary, which required parliamentary approval. Consequently, despite project approval on February 10, 2013, the signing and effectiveness of the agreement were delayed, taking place on June 3, 2018, and September 10, 2018, respectively.

The main objective of the project is to contribute to human resource development and delivery of relevant higher education. Specifically, the project aims to:
&#x2022; Improve the learning environment and quality of provision by enhancing the University&apos;s strategic policy direction for increased relevance and employability.
&#x2022; Establish an engineering faculty and state-of-the-art library.
&#x2022; Increase accommodation capacity.
&#x2022; Digitize access to learning resources.
&#x2022; Build research capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
